**No — the answer is incorrect.** The solution only considers the case where B and C lie on opposite sides of A, which gives BC = 10 (a diameter). But there's a second configuration where B and C are on the same side of A. In that case, the arc BC corresponds to the difference of the central angles, giving chord BC = 10·sin(θ_AC/2 − θ_AB/2) = 10·(16/25 − 9/25)/... = 10·(7/25)... more precisely, sin(x−y) = (4/5)(4/5) − (3/5)(3/5) = 7/25, so BC = 10·(7/25)·... — evaluating gives BC = 14/5.

The sum of all possible values is therefore 10 + 14/5 = **64/5**, which is option C, not B. The solution failed to check whether another configuration was possible.

